<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cunaxa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">401 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cunaxa was fought in 401 BCE on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> between the Persian king Artaxerxes II and his younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-younger">Cyrus the Younger</a>, who sought the throne. Cyrus' Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> routed the royal troops facing them, but Cyrus was killed charging at his brother. The stranded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>' march home, told by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anabasis">Anabasis</a>, became known as the retreat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-thousand">Ten Thousand</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cunaxa.jpg" alt="Battle of Cunaxa" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adrien Guignet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adrien_Guignet_-_Retreat_of_the_ten_thousand.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
